"smart_blocks:Assets/Put_here_hyperlinknote/JavaScript Destructuring Assignment (Arrays and Objects).md#The rest pattern “…” What if the object has more properties than we have variables? Can we take some and then assign the “rest” somewhere? We can use the rest pattern, just like we did with arrays. It’s not supported by some older browsers (IE, use Babel to polyfill it), but works in modern ones. It looks like this: ```javascript let options = { title: \"Menu\", height: 200, width: 100 }; // title = property named title // rest = object with the rest of properties let {title, ...rest} = options; // now title=\"Menu\", rest={height: 200, width: 100} alert(rest.height); // 200 alert(rest.width); // 100`": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.06446214,-0.0511934,-0.03516754,-0.04880001,0.02085217,-0.02890284,-0.04765528,0.03086896,0.07281494,-0.03244902,0.0057069,-0.01463048,-0.00942606,0.06434951,-0.00823091,-0.00881984,-0.07098264,0.08331007,-0.11679148,-0.00031349,0.10468216,-0.00081756,0.01288267,-0.02824531,0.03561746,0.05307395,0.00359496,-0.0095001,0.00631238,-0.18363991,-0.02520809,-0.05470191,-0.04386517,0.03204842,0.01353453,0.03126515,-0.02480218,0.02484883,-0.04935476,0.0731739,0.01116494,0.02883125,-0.01157772,-0.0852159,0.00090542,-0.03021785,-0.10025482,-0.01858935,0.0035424,0.0206859,-0.01360304,-0.0312438,-0.0176636,0.02000155,0.06391089,0.06714857,-0.00472544,0.09433713,0.06202481,0.05733778,0.03711843,-0.030264,-0.1155348,0.07268696,0.08427265,0.06431513,-0.01263303,0.00053095,0.03078459,0.07437535,0.00160765,0.04292883,0.00570096,0.07657911,-0.01840205,-0.02129251,0.03943365,0.01209839,0.01533808,0.00482865,-0.05518223,-0.12683062,0.0496337,-0.0191559,-0.0283009,-0.01008122,-0.00302584,0.00641268,0.03856436,0.02369081,-0.01625831,-0.08336458,0.04381043,-0.00175002,-0.05522122,-0.00458,-0.04827417,0.04078125,-0.02838872,0.10695609,-0.07228695,0.038911,0.01513097,-0.00673921,0.00825636,-0.01188753,-0.03308363,-0.00868801,0.0